@KulaHub.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5028
@clientId = 4

### List clients
GET {{KulaHub.Api_HostAddress}}/api/clients/
Accept: application/json

###

### Create contact for Dealer (ClientId 4)
### `originType` describes whether the change came from outside or inside KulaHub.
### `sourceSystemKey` identifies the external partner when known, for example `Dealer` or `Polaris`.
POST {{KulaHub.Api_HostAddress}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
	"organisationId": null,
	"firstName": "Taylor",
	"lastName": "Partner13",
	"email": "taylor.partner13@example.com",
	"postcode": "SW1A 1AA",
	//"sourceSystemKey": "Dealer",
	"originType": "InternalApp"
}

###

### Create contact for Polaris from an internal KulaHub action
POST {{KulaHub.Api_HostAddress}}/api/clients/3/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
	"organisationId": null,
	"firstName": "Jordan",
	"lastName": "Internal12",
	"email": "jordan.internal12@example.com",
	"postcode": "EC1A 1BB",
	"originType": "InternalApp"
}

###

### List contacts for Dealer after creating one
GET {{KulaHub.Api_HostAddress}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/contacts
Accept: application/json

